		<content type="html" xml:base="http://localhost/opengd77/viewtopic.php?t=2022&amp;p=17197#p17197"><![CDATA[
Perhaps there is a lot of variation in mic level between different radios.<br><br>I was told today that at 0dB on my V2.1 hardware radion, that the audio was quiter than when using my GD77.<br><br>But also other people reported that they need to set their mic gain to -6dB on the MD9600 to reduce distortion<br><br>I think I will need to change the baseline to reduce the default gain at the 0dB setting, by -6dB, but some people may then needs to increase their mic gain setting if it is too quiet<p>Statistics: Posted by <a href="http://localhost/opengd77/memberlist.php?mode=viewprofile&amp;u=50">VK3KYY</a> — Fri Jan 21, 2022 8:29 pm</p><hr />
]]></content>
